  <sharedRules>
    <rule id="ff50-7f38-5785-8e26" name="Republican Rome (AoA2) - List Notes" publicationId="fcb9-17be-94c2-bcfc" hidden="false">
      <description>ARMIES OF ANTIQUITY v2 #21 (unofficial, Martin Gibbins). This list takes the Roman army from the abandonment of the hoplite system to the end of the Republic after the wars of the triumvirs. The composition of the legion changed at an uncertain point, probably early in the second Punic war, and then existed unaltered down to the abandoning of the manipular system around the end of the second century at the time of the “Marian reforms”. For the early part of the period, we have chosen to interpret the Rorarii as identical to leves and the Accensi to be treated as camp guards and servants, and so left off table. The later period was blighted by civil wars as the political game played out, but the Romans also found time to fight the Germans, Gauls, Britons, Spanish, Numidians, Greeks, Pontics, Parthians and Egyptians amongst others! The battalion-sized cohort was now the principal formation within the legion. The main difference between this late Allies And Mercenaries: An early army may have allied contingents from the Spanish, Gallic, Pergamene, Numidian or Twilight of Greece lists (peltasts and skirmishers only). May also include 0-2 units of warriors from the Illyrian list. Allies And Mercenaries: A later army may have allied contingents from the Numidian and Twilight of Greece (peltasts and skirmishers only) lists.

ARMY COMPOSITION:
[Republican Rome]
  Cavalry: up to 25%
  Characters: up to 20%
  Legionary Infantry and Skirmishers: at least 50%
  Roman and Latin Troops: at least 40%
  Characters: up to 25% Roman and Latin Troops: At least 40% Troops may only be chosen from the Roman and Latin horse and infantry options Allies &amp; Mercenaries: Up to 50% all other troops must be allies &amp; mercenaries. Later Army (100 BC to 30 BC) – Marian &amp; Caesarian Characters: up to 20% Cavalry: Up to 25% Legionary Infantry and Skirmishers: At least 50% May not chose from the Roman and Latin Infantry section Allies: Up to 25%</description>
    </rule>
  </sharedRules>
</catalogue>
